# This corpus's prelude is populated, not committed. Its programs draw
# barcodes and assume the barcode resource is already loaded, so the
# monolithic resource is copied in as bwipp/prelude and prepended to
# every program of the corpus; it is generated and large, so it is kept
# out of the tree like the programs it serves.
#
# This file is what says so. A prelude that is part of the tree is
# there in every checkout, so its absence is a broken tree and the
# programs failing for want of it is the report; a prelude that is
# fetched is absent wherever the corpus has not been fetched, and the
# corpus is skipped instead. The evaluator tells the two apart by this
# file, so it belongs beside a prelude that fetch.sh writes and nowhere
# else.
#
# What is left below is what the evaluator prints when the prelude is
# missing, so it is addressed to whoever finds the corpus skipped.
bwipp/prelude is the monolithic barcode resource of a BWIPP checkout.
Build the monolithic resource there, then populate the corpus with it:
    BWIPP=/path/to/postscriptbarcode tests/corpus/fetch.sh bwipp
